+- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L151](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L151)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
+
+## afterModelResponse usage
+
+`afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits and receives the usage summed across every provider call in that turn — a turn that ran two tool rounds and a final round hands the hook the total of all three, not only the last ([validated by: returns the summed usage of three provider calls across two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/usageAcrossRounds.acceptance.test.ts#L68)). A round that reported no usage is skipped in the sum; a turn where no round reported any hands the hook `undefined` ([validated by: skips a round that reports no usage, and reports nothing when no round reports any](../../src/orchestration/usageAcrossRounds.acceptance.test.ts#L78)). The sum adds `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, and `totalTokens` field by field across rounds that reported ([validated by: sums token counts when both rounds reported](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L29)). When exactly one round reports, the defined value is preserved unchanged ([validated by: returns the defined value when the other round is undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L35)). When no round reports, the accumulated value is `undefined` ([validated by: returns undefined when both rounds report nothing](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L40)).
